From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <oliversargisonb@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:58:47 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 69/73] Plutonium: a Wayland client's overlay priority hint
 doesn't crash Ash

Exo's overlay_prioritizer lets any client set a surface's overlay
priority. Upstream turned the hint's use into CHECK_EQ(REGULAR) after
Lacros, its only client, went away; Chrome running as a Wayland client
sends LOW for some surfaces, and Ash aborted (surface.cc). Map LOW to
viz's kNone and REQUIRED to kRequired, as before.
---
 components/exo/surface.cc | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/exo/surface.cc b/components/exo/surface.cc
index 433a6436e6..d751e5e06c 100644
--- a/components/exo/surface.cc
+++ b/components/exo/surface.cc
@@ -1769,7 +1769,15 @@ void Surface::AppendContentsToFrame(const gfx::PointF& parent_to_root_px,
         texture_quad->set_force_rgbx();
       }
 
-      CHECK_EQ(exo::OverlayPriority::REGULAR, state_.overlay_priority_hint);
+      // Plutonium: any Wayland client may send a hint through
+      // overlay_prioritizer (Chrome's Wayland backend does), not only Lacros,
+      // which this CHECK assumed was gone: map it instead of crashing Ash.
+      if (state_.overlay_priority_hint == exo::OverlayPriority::LOW) {
+        texture_quad->overlay_priority_hint = viz::OverlayPriority::kNone;
+      } else if (state_.overlay_priority_hint ==
+                 exo::OverlayPriority::REQUIRED) {
+        texture_quad->overlay_priority_hint = viz::OverlayPriority::kRequired;
+      }
 
       if (state_.buffer.has_value() && state_.buffer->buffer() &&
           ShouldDisableOverlay(state_.buffer->buffer()->GetFormat())) {
